mario striker's battle league is coming  out on june 10th for the nintendo switch  so ahead of its release we decided to  take a look at just what exactly is  going on and the plumber's latest gaming  adventure and why everyone is battling  on a soccer pitch be sure to like the  vid and sub to the channel if you want  to stay up to date in the gaming space  now here's everything you need to know  about mario striker's battle leak  so right off the bat for those new to  mario strikers the game is part of a  series going back to the original game  for the nintendo gamecube the series  basically has mario and the usual  friends and enemies alike duking it out  through the world's most popular sport  soccer now this is not the latest fifa  or paz uh sorry e football game and for  those looking for a genuinely authentic  feeling soccer sim mario striker's  battle league will not strike that itch  but man if this game doesn't look like a  wacky good time now let's take a look at  the gameplay in its premise the shocking  and out-of-left-field violence is  honestly hilarious but just take a look  at any of the trailers and it's pretty  funny watching these characters low-key  try to murder each other all in the name  of sporting competition when i say that  the game literally encourages behavior  that would put zidane and the entire  national french soccer team of 2006 to  shame i'm being dead serious as if  that's not wild enough as is the field  itself looks like it's got electric  boundaries that you can tackle your  opponent into zapping them and leaving  them completely stunned lucky for us  though the game sees no such issue and  it doesn't implement any fouls turning  mario's soccer league looking more like  a rugged street pickup game and the back  alleys where bowser probably's got a lot  of money at stake anyone who has ever  played mario party or mario kart is  pretty well familiar with items and how  these items can be used to give  themselves an advantageous boost or to  wreck their opponents usually in pretty  hilarious ways that mechanic is also  present in mario strikers and it all  ties back into the tackling i mentioned  earlier although if you were just  trucking your opponent left and right  don't expect to also get a bunch of  items because as fun as that sounds it's  not exactly fair is it that's why  players who just got rocked will have  the benefit of receiving items to give  them a fair shot the game's got a  distinct flair and personality to it  even in the stadium selection the  stadiums are often two different arenas  just smashed together at the midfield  line making a functional hybrid of both  now the fields themselves might be  different in their size but the  difference is usually very minor the  main draw though is watching the huge  landmasses crash into each other before  the players take the field ready to  embarrass their opponents the core  gameplay loop is more similar to  something you'd see in fifa street or  volta mode than a full 11v11 match in  mario strikers you've got a steady  roster of 10 characters to choose from  to play in four v4 matches each  character will have different stats such  as power or speed with characters like  princess peach being on the lighter side  and huge bruisers like bowser or wario  having far more power but at the expense  of being much slower you can pass and  shoot as well as take some detours  towards question blocks that appear on  the field really what distinguishes the  gameplay from a regular soccer match are  special shots that players can take  after a team has built up enough power  consider these shots like the blue  shells of mario strikers but with more  skill involved activating a special shot  brings up a swinging meter similar to  those that you might have seen in mario  golf games if you pull a perfectly timed  shot an unblockable shot launches across  the field guaranteeing you a score don't  worry though if you missed the timing  window you could still potentially make  the shot but it is possible for the  other team to stop it truthfully these  special moves look varied too each  highlighting a character's unique trait  and they're also a really cool visual  flourish like a final smash almost  showing off elements of the sketchy ink  style that appears in the official  artwork the characters post goal  celebrations as seen through cinematic  and replay cameras all add extra flair  and they're a fun touch now since the  roster is fairly thin at 10 characters  there's a great emphasis on gear to help  add more playstyle variety like the  special shots the different gear are  nice visual touches that factor in a  character's style and traits mario's  headgear for example are a series of  different armor takes on his iconic hat  each with a stat boost so you can tweak  your player to your liking now this  seems to be where the game's economy  comes most into play since the way that  you get new gear is by paying with coins  now getting coins is simple just play  the game customization also extends a  bit to your soccer club too with things  like different fence posts and  decorations managing your club is part  of the backdrop of competitive play as  you'll make your own club identity by  picking a logo from a series of icons  background shields and colors now if all  this sounds good to you and you decide  to take the plunge nintendo has  announced plans for multiple free  content drops such as additional  characters post launch mario striker's  battle league will release on june 10th  for nintendo switch  now be sure to stick to game spot for  all things gaming and if you're a  nintendo fan keep an eye out for my  coverage of pokemon violin and scarlet  coming up as well as our breath of the  wild expert max breaking down elite  combat tips and a bunch of things that  you didn't know that's it for me until  next time  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

